/P 107 0 R
/T (Across the dataset, women were consistently described as mediators, counsellors, mobilizers and protectors of social cohesion. Their social relationships and responsibility for family welfare often position them as first responders when tensions emerge as they engage in family-level negotiation, reconciliation, peace caravans and community dialogue well before formal institutions become involved.)
/E (Across the dataset, women were consistently described as mediators, counsellors, mobilizers and protectors of social cohesion. Their social relationships and responsibility for family welfare often position them as first responders when tensions emerge as they engage in family-level negotiation, reconciliation, peace caravans and community dialogue well before formal institutions become involved.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
