/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 107 0 R
/T (This pattern was reported consistently by key informants across all four study countries i.e. Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa, thus indicating a shared regional dynamic rather than a localized effect. This finding is strongly corroborated by UN Women's documentation of Kenyan women peacebuilders such as Mary Mariach and Christine Lemuya, who mediate longstanding inter-tribal disputes in Kenya's ASAL regions through local dialogue and outreach, using approaches that, per UN Women's reporting, male-dominated leadership structures have not always been willing to take \(UN Women, 2022\).)
/E (This pattern was reported consistently by key informants across all four study countries i.e. Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa, thus indicating a shared regional dynamic rather than a localized effect. This finding is strongly corroborated by UN Women's documentation of Kenyan women peacebuilders such as Mary Mariach and Christine Lemuya, who mediate longstanding inter-tribal disputes in Kenya's ASAL regions through local dialogue and outreach, using approaches that, per UN Women's reporting, male-dominated leadership structures have not always been willing to take \(UN Women, 2022\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
