<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 625 0 R
/E (Support community-led cross-border peace platforms - back elder and community-driven models such as the Ateker Leaders' Council, established in December 2025 across Kenya, Uganda, South Sudan and Ethiopia, as a template for combining community legitimacy with formal state and regional backing \(CEWARN, 2025\).)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 626 0 R
/E (Embed women specifically within cross-border platforms - ensure emerging cross-border coordination bodies and community councils include formal seats for women mediators from their founding stage, rather than adding women's representation after a platform's structure is already fixed.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 112 0 R
/T (3. Context-Specific Barriers)
/E (3. Context-Specific Barriers)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 627 0 R
/E (Prioritize land and resource rights reform in Kenya and Tanzania - address land tenure specifically, since it is the dominant barrier to women's participation identified in these contexts, distinct from the clan-based exclusion pattern found in Somalia.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 628 0 R
/E (Prioritize formal representation within and alongside clan-based structures in Somalia - design participation mechanisms that engage clan governance directly rather than assuming a single national model will work across both land-tenure-driven and clan-structure-driven contexts.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 112 0 R
/T (4. Sustaining Women's Existing Mediation Work)
/E (4. Sustaining Women's Existing Mediation Work)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 629 0 R
/E (Fund and professionalize women's mediation networks - provide sustained financial and technical support to existing women's mediation networks and peace caravans, building on models such as for example the Marsabit Women's Mediation Network, rather than creating parallel structures.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 630 0 R
/E (Invest in the preconditions for participation - address literacy, financial dependence, mobility constraints and unpaid care burdens directly, since these were identified as primary barriers to women's formal participation independent of any change in governance structures.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
