1201 0 obj
<<
/Title (The evidence in this brief points to a specific and actionable policy gap: pastoralist women are already doing the practical work of peacebuilding and, in many cases, natural-resource stewardship but formal governance architecture has not caught up with that reality. Where deliberate institutional reform has taken place, as in Ethiopia's participatory rangeland management programme or Kenya's supported peace-committee network, the result has been measurable gains in both women's participation and the quality of governance and peace outcomes. The policy task is therefore not to build a case for why women should be included the evidence for that case is already strong but to replicate, adapt and scale the specific institutional mechanisms that have been shown to convert informal contribution into formal authority.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1192 0 R
>>
endobj
